# Code owners for this repository.
#
# `@catincloudlabs` is a USER account, not the `catincloud-labs` organization
# that owns this repository. CODEOWNERS resolves users and teams; an
# organization name on its own is not a valid owner, and this organization has
# no teams, so a `@catincloud-labs/<team>` entry would resolve to nothing
# silently.
#
# The second owner is named on the SEAM, not on `*`. From 2026-08-23 to
# 2026-09-04 `*` carried both owners, and every pull request here -- docs,
# Dependabot bumps, CI plumbing -- requested a review from the upstream
# maintainer; none of those requests was answered, and each one made the next
# less legible. A request that fires only when a file binding this package to
# dex-core changes carries information: it says the seam moved. Everything
# else stays owner-only, which is the same posture as the other repositories
# in this organisation, where the owner can only bypass.
#
# The seam is: the dex-core pin and the entry point that dex-core resolves
# (`pyproject.toml`); the bridge module, the only import of dex-core in `src/`
# (`dex.py`); the tests that import the real package; and the two tests that
# hold the pin and the entry point to their declared values without importing
# it. `tests/test_conformance.py` is this package's own suite and imports
# nothing from dex-core, so it is not the seam. Re-derive the import half
# rather than trusting it (a docstring mentioning the package is not a seam):
#   grep -rlE '^\s*(from|import) exmergo_dex_core' src tests

